---
/**
 * Site-use terms.
 *
 * The legal publisher has not been established yet, so this page avoids inventing an
 * entity, address, jurisdiction, or contractual contact channel.
 */
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '@config/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`Terms for using ${SITE.domain}, including content use, third-party links and the current publisher status.`}
  effectiveDate={LEGAL.effectiveDate}
  lastUpdated={LEGAL.lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="lead">
    These terms describe permitted use of the {SITE.name} website at{' '}
    <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong>. The site is currently published without a publicly stated
    legal entity or business contact channel; those details will be added before commercial
    advertising or visitor-submission features are enabled.
  </p>

  <h2 id="permitted-use">1. Permitted use</h2>
  <p>
    You may access and use the site for lawful, personal and internal business purposes. Do not
    interfere with the site, attempt unauthorized access, transmit harmful material, or reuse
    substantial portions of its content in a way that misrepresents the original source.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content-and-attribution">2. Content and attribution</h2>
  <p>
    Content is published under the StackPipeline organization byline. It is provided for
    general information and is not legal, financial, security, tax or professional advice.
    Software features, prices and terms change frequently; verify material decisions directly
    with the relevant vendor before relying on a guide or comparison.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party-links">3. Third-party links and affiliate relationships</h2>
  <p>
    The site may link to third-party websites that StackPipeline does not control. Those sites
    have their own terms and privacy practices. Some links may be affiliate links; see the{' '}
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> for how that relationship is
    described.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability-and-changes">4. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The site may be changed, paused or removed without notice. We do not promise that every
    page will be complete, current, error-free or continuously available. Material changes to
    these terms will be reflected in the date at the top of this page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="publisher-status">5. Publisher status and contact</h2>
  <p>
    A verified legal entity, mailing address and public contact method have not yet been
    configured. This page is not a substitute for the jurisdiction-specific terms that will be
    published once those details are established. Until then, do not send personal information
    through a channel represented as StackPipeline.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
